description: Always store and reference website images as .webp
alwaysApply: true
---

# Auto WebP images

- All website images under `images/` must be `.webp`.
- Never commit or leave `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.gif`, `.bmp`, `.tif`, `.tiff`, or `.avif` in `images/`.
- After adding or downloading any raster image, run `npm run convert:webp` (or let the watcher / git hook / Cursor hook convert it).
- HTML/JS/CSS `src`, `href`, `data-src`, and CSS `url(...)` must use `.webp` paths.
- Favicon / apple-touch-icon must use `images/kodam-kitchen-logo.webp` with `type="image/webp"`.
- For continuous auto-convert while dropping files into `images/`, run `npm run watch:webp`.
